-- test: a `via` function that reads `Clock.now` would launder the timing of its callers through the policy (ADR 0116 amendment of 2026-11-09, C7, `spec/07 §5` rule 7): `show` calls the policy before and after work on a `secret`, so the reading's `L_clk` is `secret`, and the reading inside `stamp_it` is U4001; without the rule `una check` accepted it and the run printed the elapsed time
-- spec: spec/07 §5
-- expect: error U4001 at src/release.una:15:13
module main

import release (stamp_of)

work(n: secret Int) -> secret Int = n * n

pub show(n: secret Int) -> Unit
  uses @console: Console[print]
  uses @clock: Clock[now]
=
  let start = stamp_of(0)
  let squared = work(n)
  let stop = stamp_of(0)
  @console.print("{stop - start} ms")
